    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1244">

                <pb facs="1134" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg876"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of your letter of the 10th instant, with which you enclosed
                    copies of the letters addressed to the Navy Department by the commanding officer
                        <pb facs="1135" n="877" xml:id="pg877"/> of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Iroquois</hi> in November 1861, regarding the movements
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">Sumter</hi> in the port of Martinique.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inquire whether the action of Commander Palmer of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Iroquois</hi> in communicating with the shore and
                    arranging for signals as to the movements of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sumter</hi>, as indicated in his reports, received the approval or
                    disapproval of the Navy Department at the time.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
